  <prompt>Resolve the B04 multi-tenant Dataverse routing gap surfaced by task 202 SESSION 5 Lesson 3: `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:37-39` reads ONE `Dataverse:ServiceUrl` from config at DI-setup time, contradicting Model 1's per-tenant Dataverse design intent. FIRST STEP: author an ADR Tension row in `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md` §ADR Tensions per root CLAUDE.md §6.5 three-path protocol (Path A documented exception / Path B ADR amendment / Path C pivot to comply). STOP and escalate to owner for path choice — this is a legitimate stopping condition per §6.5, not a skill failure. On owner decision: apply chosen path (Path A ≈ 1h doc-only, Path B ≈ 16-40h ADR amendment + `DataverseServiceClientImpl` refactor for runtime multi-tenant routing + I5 ArchTest extension + tests, Path C scope-uncertain — may spawn additional tasks for Model 1 architectural refactor).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform architect. Expert in: root CLAUDE.md §6.5 ADR Conflict Resolution Protocol (mandatory three-path template + escalation format); ADR-027 subscription-isolation-and-dataverse-solution-management + Model 1 shared-tier documented exception (per project spec.md §ADR Tensions Path A rows); project design.md D3 tenancy model + §5.2 handler placement rules; `DataverseServiceClientImpl` + `DataverseServiceClient` factory + token cache patterns (`RegistrationDataverseService` cross-env token cache reference); Model 1 vs Model 2 Dataverse topology (Model 1 shared tier: one BFF, N tenants; Model 2 dedicated: one BFF per env).</role>

  <goal>ONE of the three §6.5 paths is chosen by the owner and fully executed:
- **Path A**: `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md` §ADR Tensions has a new row documenting the multi-tenant DV routing exception with concrete rationale + impact + rejected alternatives; `design.md` §Placement Justification references the exception; PR description explicitly cites path A + code-review approves; NO code change to `DataverseServiceClientImpl`.
- **Path B**: A new ADR-XXX amendment file exists (concise + full versions), extending prior DV-client scoping guidance to permit runtime multi-tenant routing; `DataverseServiceClientImpl` refactored to accept per-request/per-tenant `ServiceUrl` (via `ITenantContextAccessor` or equivalent seam); token cache adapted for per-tenant scoping; I5 ArchTest (`Spaarke.ArchTests.TenantIsolation.I5_*`) extended to cover the new routing surface; unit + integration tests green; publish size + delta reported.
- **Path C**: Model 1 architecture refactored to comply with single-DV-per-tier assumption; additional POMLs spawned for scope beyond this task; `DataverseServiceClientImpl` left unchanged; H5 handler behavior amended to NOT create per-tenant Dataverse envs in Model 1.

Regardless of path: the ADR-tension row exists in `spec.md` per §6.5 mandatory-format; task 202's punch list B04 row is annotated with `applied — Path X`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>SESSION 5 (2026-08-24) surfaced this during Model 1 Prod BFF standup: `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:37-39` reads a single `Dataverse:ServiceUrl` from `IConfiguration` at DI-setup time via `IOptions<DataverseOptions>`. This is fine for Model 2 (one BFF per dedicated env — env=1:1 with URL). For Model 1 (shared tier: one BFF serves N tenants), it contradicts the spec.md D3 tenancy design intent that each tenant has its OWN Dataverse environment created by H5. Either:
- **Path A reality**: Model 1 shared BFF actually serves ONE shared Dataverse per tier (all Model 1 customers share `sprksharedstartus2` for now), and the multi-tenant story is a future goal not a v3.6 reality. Document the exception.
- **Path B reality**: H5 DOES create per-tenant Dataverse envs in Model 1 (per current spec), so `DataverseServiceClientImpl` genuinely needs runtime routing. Requires ADR amendment (which ADR? candidates: ADR-027 sub-isolation, ADR-028 spaarke-auth-architecture — DV client scoping is auth-adjacent).
- **Path C reality**: The spec's Model 1 per-tenant DV design is wrong; walk it back; shared DV IS the Model 1 design.

**Why this must go through §6.5**: silent compliance (leaving single-URL wiring) may produce a Model 1 tenant-isolation bug at runtime; silent extension (patching `DataverseServiceClientImpl` for multi-tenant without ADR amendment) may violate implicit ADR-027/ADR-028 assumptions. Neither is acceptable per §6.5 — the choice must be surfaced explicitly.

**Owner input is load-bearing**: only the project owner can choose between "Model 1 shared DV is the design, spec should walk back the per-tenant claim" (Path C) vs "Model 1 per-tenant DV is the design, extend the client" (Path B) vs "narrow exception for v3.6" (Path A).</background>
