  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, opus/xhigh). Read root CLAUDE.md §6.5 in full (ADR Conflict Resolution Protocol — the format is mandatory). Read `.claude/adr/ADR-027` + `ADR-028`. Read `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B04 row + Class-B verification matrix entry.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Verify current state">Grep-verify `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:37-39` still reads single `Dataverse:ServiceUrl` via `IOptions<DataverseOptions>`. Read the full file. Read `DataverseOptions.cs`. Enumerate all injection sites (services that receive `DataverseServiceClientImpl` or its interface) — this scope determines the blast radius for Path B refactor.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Author ADR tension row + ESCALATE">Add a new row to `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md` §ADR Tensions section using the exact §6.5 template:

🔔 **ADR Conflict — Resolution Required**
- **ADR in question**: ADR-027 (sub-isolation) + ADR-028 (auth) — DV client scoping is auth-adjacent
- **Specific rule**: [quote the relevant MUST from the chosen ADR — likely ADR-027's per-tenant DV isolation intent OR ADR-028's per-tenant auth scope]
- **Conflict**: `DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:37-39` reads ONE `Dataverse:ServiceUrl` at DI-setup, contradicts Model 1 per-tenant DV design (D3)
- **Proposed path**: request owner input — this task cannot self-select
- **Rationale for each path**: A (documented exception if shared-DV is v3.6 reality), B (ADR amendment + runtime routing if per-tenant is true design), C (walk back spec if shared-DV is the intended design)
- **Impact if A**: none (documentation-only); if B: ~16-40h refactor + I5 ArchTest extension + amendment authoring; if C: additional spec/design amendments + potentially H5 behavior change
- **Alternative considered (and rejected)**: silent single-URL wiring (produces cross-tenant data-leak potential in Model 1)

**STOP HERE**. Escalation trigger fires: `owner-decision-required`. Notify owner via chat + set task status to `paused-awaiting-owner-decision`. Do NOT proceed to Step 3 without owner path selection.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Path A execute (only if chosen)">Author documented-exception content in `design.md` §Placement Justification citing rationale + concrete v3.6 scope. Update PR description with §6.5 exception citation. Annotate `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` B04 row: `applied — Path A — see spec.md §ADR Tensions row X`. NO code change to `DataverseServiceClientImpl`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Path B execute (only if chosen)">Author `.claude/adr/ADR-XXX-multi-tenant-dataverse-routing.md` (concise) + `docs/adr/ADR-XXX-...` (full). Refactor `DataverseServiceClientImpl` to accept per-request/per-tenant `ServiceUrl` via new seam (`ITenantDataverseUrlResolver` or extend existing `ITenantContextAccessor`). Adapt token cache for per-tenant scoping (reuse `RegistrationDataverseService` cross-env pattern). Extend `Spaarke.ArchTests.TenantIsolation.I5_*` ArchTest to cover new routing surface. Unit + integration tests. Report BFF publish size + delta. Annotate B04 row: `applied — Path B — ADR-XXX + code refactor`.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Path C execute (only if chosen)">Amend spec.md D3 tenancy model to walk back per-tenant DV claim for Model 1. Amend H5 handler behavior via a new POML in this project. Annotate B04 row: `applied — Path C — spec walked back; see amendment + spawn tasks`. Notify owner that Path C spawns additional work.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Build + verify (Path B only)">`dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` — 0 warnings 0 errors. `dotnet test` green. `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/` — record compressed size + delta vs 44.96 MB baseline.</step>
    <step order="6.5" name="Quality gates">FULL rigor + BFF-touched (Path B) → invoke `code-review` + `adr-check` skills per root CLAUDE.md §8. Address any Critical findings. `adr-check` should FIND the new ADR-XXX and validate the amendment format.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Report">Update `current-task.md` + `TASK-INDEX.md` + `notes/task-202-punch-list.md` verification matrix B04 outcome. Cross-reference the spec.md ADR-tension row + chosen path from PR description.</step>
