  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing overlap — `DataverseServiceClientImpl` already exists; this task modifies it (Path B) OR documents an exception (Path A) OR amends spec (Path C). Extension — Path B introduces new tenant-URL-resolver seam; alternative was in-place per-tenant tokens per-tenant which fails the extension test (that IS the refactor). Cost-of-doing-nothing — silent single-URL wiring in Model 1 shared BFF produces cross-tenant Dataverse-data-leak potential at runtime; concrete failure mode named.

This task is INTENTIONALLY foundational + serial + owner-gated. The value is NOT in code shipped — it's in the ADR-tension resolution ceremony being followed correctly. Silent compliance with a MUST rule that produces cross-tenant data leaks would itself be a §6.5 protocol violation.</notes>

